      "text": "We are to solve for the value of the pencils, denoted as $x$, in the given equations.\n\n**Equation:**\n1. $4P + 3x = 224$\n2. $2P + 5x = 154$\n\n**Step by step explanation:**\n\nTo solve these equations simultaneously:\n\n1. Subtract equation (2) from equation (1):\n   $4P + 3x - (2P + 5x) = 224 - 154$\n\n2. This simplifies to:\n   $2P - 2x = 70$\n\n3. Divide by 2 to isolate $P - x$:\n   $P - x = 35$\n\n4. Let, $n$ be the price of one pen as:\n   $P = 35 + n$\n\n5. Substitute $P$ back into equation (1), treating $x$ as a single variable:\n   $4(35 + n) + 3x = 224$\n   $140 + 4n + 3x = 224$\n\n6. Isolate $3x$:\n   $3x = 224 - 140 - 4n$\n   $3x = 84 - 4n$\n\n7. Substitute $x$ back into the equation (2):\n   $2(35 + n) + 5x = 154$\n   $70 + 2n + 5x = 154$\n\n8. Match and eliminate $n$:\n   $5x = 154 - 70 - 2n$\n   $5x = 84 - 2n$\n\n9. Solve for $x$ using $3x$:\n   $x = \\frac{84 - 2n}{5}$\n\n10. Substitute $x$ from (9) into equation (3):\n    $n + \\frac{84 - 2n}{5}\\geqslant 35$\n\n11. Distribute $\\frac{84 - 2n}{5}$:\n    $n + \\frac{84}{5} - \\frac{2n}{5} \\geqslant 35$\n\n12. Multiply by 5 to clear the fraction:\n    $5n + 84 - 2n \\geqslant 175$\n\n13. Solve for $n$:\n    $3n + 84 \\geqslant 175$\n    $3n \\geqslant 91$\n    $n \\geqslant \\frac{91}{3}$\n    $n \\geqslant 30.33$\n\nSince price is an integer, we round to the nearest whole number, which gives $n = 30$. On substituting, we find:\n     $3x = 84 - 2(30)$\n     $3x = 24$\n\nThus, the cost of a pencil is $\\boxed{8}$.",
